OL,3,AChinese artist jailed over satirical
OL,4,AMao sculptures, say rights groups
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Chinese artist known for his
OL,7,Fsatirical sculptures of Mao Zedong has
OL,8,Fbeen handed a maximum three-year jail
OL,9,Fterm for "slandering China's heroes",
OL,10,Faccording to rights groups.
OL,12,FA court in Hebei province had ruled on
OL,13,FTuesday that Gao Zhen's work "infringes
OL,14,Fupon the hero's reputation and harms
OL,15,Fpublic interest".
OL,17,FAmong the 70-year-old's most famous
OL,18,Fpieces, produced with his brother Gao
OL,19,FQiang, is a sculpture comprising a
OL,20,Fsquad of Mao-like figures holding Jesus
OL,21,FChrist at gunpoint.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
